71
00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.860
Tim, we always ask people how they got their job on The Office.

72
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.400
And you originally, you were offered the role and you turned it down, right?

73
00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.960
Yes, that is true.

74
00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.420
I wouldn't say turned it down.

75
00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.360
I didn't turn it down to Greg and Michael Short.

76
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.240
I turned it down to my manager.

77
00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.640
Like, he called and said, like, oh, we got this offer for this episode.

78
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.160
And I was like, no, I don't know.

79
00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.900
I don't know if I should do it or not.

80
00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.420
Because I actually was, you know, honestly, I was hoping to get paid more.

81
00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.740
We had no money.

82
00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.080
It was in the very beginning.

83
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.220
It was the second season, I think.

84
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.620
Early in the second season.

85
00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:43.060
And NBC was not, you know, they were, like, not into paying me more money.

86
00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.880
And so I passed.

87
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.160
And I just told my agent, right?

88
00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:54.220
And then my manager's assistant called me back on his personal phone and said, I really

89
00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.400
think you should do this.

90
00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.400
And I don't make these kind of calls all the time.

91
00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.260
But I think that this is, like, one of those comedies that everybody in the industry watches.

92
00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.580
And I think you should do it.

93
00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.020
And I knew Steven.

94
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.100
And I knew some of the other people involved in the show, too.

95
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.280
So I was just like, okay, yeah, I'll do it, you know.

96
00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.920
But it would have been nice if they came back and begged me, like, you know, to have

97
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.940
Michael Schur come back and go, hey, Tim, come on, please do the show.

98
00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.180
But that never happened.

99
00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:25.060
Well, you know, Tim, you were our very first, quote, unquote, stunt casting.

100
00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.380
You were our first name actor to come on the show.

101
00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.100
It was a big thing.

102
00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.960
It was a big buzz.

103
00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:33.520
Yes.

104
00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:40.380
I do remember I was very flattered, actually, because I'd say almost everybody in the cast

105
00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.160
came by because we weren't on the regular office set.

106
00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.000
We were at the Chili set.

107
00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:51.040
And I think I kind of remember a lot of people coming by to say hello because I was there

108
00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.940
and I was pretty impressed by that.

109
00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.480
God, I wish I'd have taken pictures and stuff like we do now, you know.

110
00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:56.980
Right.

111
00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:57.400
I know.

112
00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:58.000
I know.

113
00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.520
I didn't do any of that.

114
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.720
There's fantastic bloopers from that day, too, for folks that get the DVDs.

115
00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:09.580
I mean, when you come in and sing, I know you're scripted to come in at the end of the

116
00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.880
line, you know, but when you start singing that, I want my baby back, baby back, and

117
00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.160
then Steve comes in, Chili's.

118
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:17.900
It's so great.

119
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:23.640
And we had Melora on the podcast, and there she is seated between the two of you.

120
00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.440
And she said it was like one of the hardest things she's ever had to do is not laugh.

121
00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:28.200
Yeah.

122
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.820
In the very beginning, I remember we were trying to do it, and Stephen was going like, he would

123
00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.360
start going, I want my baby back, baby back.

124
00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:41.980
And then I would join in with him, and then he would start singing it, but I would lose

125
00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.640
