126
00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.060
And I was like, I don't, it's a commercial.

127
00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:50.300
I can't, I don't know how to sing a commercial, you know.

128
00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:58.640
So it was really fun, because we started laughing at the absurdity of two grown men singing that

129
00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.420
song at the Chili's.

130
00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.540
Like, I was laughing at that alone.

131
00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:03.580
I thought it was so funny.

132
00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:09.020
And then these two guys are somewhat like each other, you know, like you expected Christian

133
00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.580
to be this kind of like, you know, city worker dude.

134
00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.980
But then, you know, he had all of these like private issues that came out during lunch, you

135
00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.380
know, like his mother being ill and stuff like that.

136
00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:24.080
Yeah, he overshared just the way Michael overshares.

137
00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.280
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

138
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.800
Was it just one day of work?

139
00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.580
Did you guys get it all in one day?

140
