01:25:57.370 --> 01:25:58.810
I usually take the stairs.

2025
01:25:59.070 --> 01:26:00.930
I just thought I would give myself a treat.

2026
01:26:01.710 --> 01:26:02.810
I meant your audition.

2027
01:26:04.470 --> 01:26:12.910
I just feel like the chances of this working out are slim to none, you know, or none to none.

2028
01:26:15.040 --> 01:26:19.380
Like they start at none and then they just stay there.

2029
01:26:19.640 --> 01:26:21.300
That is not nice.

2030
01:26:24.970 --> 01:26:26.110
I'm going to take the stairs.

2031
01:26:32.280 --> 01:26:34.560
I have a lot to say about this deleted scene.

2032
01:26:34.860 --> 01:26:35.380
Okay.

2033
01:26:35.800 --> 01:26:36.880
And here it is.

2034
01:26:37.570 --> 01:26:42.820
It bothered me in this episode that Pete didn't just say the truth.

2035
01:26:43.800 --> 01:26:48.720
So in the shooting draft when he approaches her at the elevator and he kind of fumbles through this.

2036
01:26:49.000 --> 01:26:49.140
Yeah.

2037
01:26:49.140 --> 01:26:50.860
He says this is never going to happen, right?

2038
01:26:50.940 --> 01:26:51.900
We just listen to it.

2039
01:26:52.520 --> 01:26:54.300
Then he would have changed tactics.

2040
01:26:54.500 --> 01:26:56.400
He would have been like, okay, that didn't work.

2041
01:26:56.600 --> 01:27:03.300
But Pete in the shooting draft is determined to prevent her from going alone to Clark's apartment.

2042
01:27:03.480 --> 01:27:05.680
And he comes up with this kind of ruse.

2043
01:27:06.040 --> 01:27:06.160
Yeah.

2044
01:27:06.180 --> 01:27:11.240
Instead of calling out Clark as being a creeper, he just makes sure that Erin is not alone.

2045
01:27:11.460 --> 01:27:13.000
Well, that's all fine and good, Angela.

2046
01:27:13.000 --> 01:27:15.200
But I wish he would have just said the truth.

2047
01:27:15.760 --> 01:27:18.940
We don't need to protect the creepers, I guess, is my point.

2048
01:27:19.140 --> 01:27:19.980
Oh, absolutely.

2049
01:27:20.280 --> 01:27:25.360
But I did want to show that he was trying throughout this to deter her.

2050
01:27:26.220 --> 01:27:31.200
Ultimately, what happens is Andy, Pete, and Erin show up to Clark's apartment.

2051
01:27:31.800 --> 01:27:32.020
Yes.

2052
01:27:32.200 --> 01:27:33.880
Andy is now the co-anchor.

2053
01:27:34.060 --> 01:27:34.520
Yes.

2054
01:27:34.760 --> 01:27:37.100
And he's taking his job very seriously.

2055
01:27:37.400 --> 01:27:40.600
I love it when Clark's like, I think you guys got it.

2056
01:27:40.660 --> 01:27:41.840
And Andy's like, no, I didn't.

2057
01:27:41.840 --> 01:27:42.620
I don't got it.

2058
01:27:42.900 --> 01:27:43.560
She did great.

2059
01:27:43.720 --> 01:27:44.220
She did great.

2060
01:27:44.360 --> 01:27:45.340
I need a close-up.

2061
01:27:45.440 --> 01:27:46.460
I need you to go in tighter.

2062
01:27:46.900 --> 01:27:47.060
Yeah.

2063
01:27:47.240 --> 01:27:49.060
Erin, why don't you go have dinner with Pete?

2064
01:27:49.500 --> 01:27:51.480
All of this backfires for Clark.

2065
01:27:51.900 --> 01:27:55.320
And it also shows how Andy doesn't see Aaron.

2066
01:27:55.540 --> 01:27:57.560
He just sees himself always.

2067
01:27:57.940 --> 01:27:58.280
Yeah.

2068
01:27:58.420 --> 01:28:01.520
I did appreciate the reveals of this storyline.

2069
01:28:02.100 --> 01:28:06.840
Well, I'll have you know Clark's apartment was located on Kester Avenue in Sherman Oaks.

2070
01:28:06.960 --> 01:28:10.500
We shot these scenes after all of the stuff at Roy's house.

2071
01:28:10.500 --> 01:28:13.020
It was a really big day for our crew.

2072
01:28:13.260 --> 01:28:18.620
They had to do what is called a company move, where they pack up everything from one location

2073
01:28:18.620 --> 01:28:20.640
and move to a second location.

2074
01:28:21.000 --> 01:28:22.240
It's a big deal.

2075
01:28:22.400 --> 01:28:24.040
So this was a long day for them.

2076
01:28:24.180 --> 01:28:26.940
It was a long day, and it was triple digits outside.

2077
01:28:27.200 --> 01:28:27.400
Yeah.

2078
01:28:27.400 --> 01:28:32.020
And then the diner that we shot at, we did actually shoot this on a different day.

2079
01:28:32.200 --> 01:28:35.700
This was The Hungry Fox on Sherman Way in Van Nuys.

2080
01:28:35.860 --> 01:28:37.340
It is right by our studio.

2081
01:28:37.560 --> 01:28:39.120
It was Greg's favorite place.

2082
01:28:39.300 --> 01:28:44.220
He would go there in the mornings before work and eat breakfast and go over his notes and do his thinking,

2083
01:28:44.220 --> 01:28:45.940
and then he would come into work.

2084
01:28:46.140 --> 01:28:49.040
We also shot some Roy Pam scenes there.

2085
01:28:49.240 --> 01:28:50.520
It's really good food.

2086
01:28:50.520 --> 01:28:54.840
I have to tell you, one morning I was driving into work, and I went early.

2087
01:28:54.840 --> 01:29:02.200
I was very pregnant, and I just was like, I want a big, big breakfast before I even walk onto set.

2088
01:29:02.900 --> 01:29:04.420
So I got up really early.

2089
01:29:04.540 --> 01:29:06.940
I wasn't sleeping great anyway towards the end of your pregnancy.

2090
01:29:07.120 --> 01:29:08.340
You know you don't really sleep great.

2091
01:29:08.340 --> 01:29:16.260
And I went to The Hungry Fox so early, and I ordered myself this huge breakfast, and in walked Greg.

2092
01:29:16.480 --> 01:29:16.680
Yeah.

2093
01:29:16.860 --> 01:29:18.740
And he was like, hey, Ange, what are you doing here?

2094
01:29:18.780 --> 01:29:20.200
I was like, I was just really hungry.

2095
01:29:21.440 --> 01:29:23.440
And so we had breakfast together.

2096
01:29:23.840 --> 01:29:25.760
Well, everyone, that was Roy's wedding.

2097
01:29:26.020 --> 01:29:29.860
A big thank you to Tim Meadows for joining us.

2098
01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:32.220
Everybody, please go see our Mean Girls movie.

2099
01:29:32.340 --> 01:29:33.540
It opens this Friday.

2100
01:29:33.760 --> 01:29:36.120
We had so much fun making it.

2101
01:29:36.120 --> 01:29:39.760
And, oh, my gosh, I'm excited to see it on the big screen.

2102
01:29:39.980 --> 01:29:41.060
I'm so excited.

2103
01:29:41.320 --> 01:29:42.560
My daughter's so excited.

2104
01:29:42.700 --> 01:29:44.340
A bunch of her friends are going to see it.

2105
01:29:44.580 --> 01:29:45.860
Jenna, this is so fun.

2106
01:29:46.040 --> 01:29:47.060
It's my big moment.

2107
01:29:47.200 --> 01:29:47.940
It's a big moment.

2108
01:29:48.480 --> 01:29:54.820
And also, of course, thank you to Steve Burgess and to all of you for writing in with your questions and your great observations.

2109
01:29:55.240 --> 01:29:57.900
Yes, and I would say thank you to Miles McNutt.

2110
01:29:58.200 --> 01:29:58.620
Aw.

2111
01:29:58.880 --> 01:30:03.220
For two years of awesome reviews that were always interesting, if not hilarious.

2112
01:30:03.560 --> 01:30:05.220
We'll be looking for you in the comments.

2113
01:30:05.320 --> 01:30:05.800
That's right.

2114
01:30:06.120 --> 01:30:07.420
We'll see you guys next week.

2115
01:30:07.560 --> 01:30:08.020
See you then.

2116
01:30:15.120 --> 01:30:16.940
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

